  <section>
    <p class="post-lead"><strong>Short answer:</strong> nothing is deleted. Your account, chats, files and channel subscriptions all survive an expired Premium untouched. You simply stop having the Premium features — uploads drop back to 2 GB, ads return in public channels, and doubled limits revert. Renewing restores everything instantly, with no migration and no setup.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What you lose the moment it expires</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>4 GB uploads → 2 GB.</strong> New files above 2 GB can no longer be sent.</li>
      <li><strong>Download throttling returns</strong> on large files.</li>
      <li><strong>Sponsored messages come back</strong> in public channels.</li>
      <li><strong>Doubled limits revert</strong> — folders, pinned chats, channel subscriptions, saved GIFs, public usernames.</li>
      <li><strong>Premium badge and name colour</strong> disappear from your profile.</li>
      <li><strong>Animated profile video</strong> reverts to a static photo.</li>
      <li><strong>Custom emoji</strong> can no longer be used in messages.</li>
      <li><strong>Voice-to-text transcription</strong> and real-time chat translation stop working.</li>
      <li><strong>Telegram Business features</strong> switch off — greeting messages, quick replies, opening hours.</li>
      <li><strong>Channel boosts you were providing</strong> are withdrawn, which can drop a channel below its boost level.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What stays exactly as it was</h2>
    <p>This is the part people worry about unnecessarily:</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Your account</strong> — nothing is suspended or restricted.</li>
      <li><strong>All chats and message history</strong>, unchanged.</li>
      <li><strong>Files you already sent</strong>, including ones over 2 GB. They remain downloadable.</li>
      <li><strong>Folders and channels above the free limit</strong> stay; you just cannot add new ones until you are back under it.</li>
      <li><strong>Stickers and custom emoji packs</strong> remain in your account, temporarily unusable rather than lost.</li>
      <li><strong>Your Stars balance</strong> — completely unaffected. Stars and Premium are separate products.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Renewing from Uzbekistan</h2>
    <p>The obstacle is the same one as buying it the first time: Telegram's own checkout — App Store, Google Play or @PremiumBot — wants an international card, and Uzcard and Humo are not that.</p>
    <p>Through StarsJoy the renewal takes 2–3 minutes:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>Open <a href="https://telegram.me/starsjoybot" target="_blank" rel="noopener">@starsjoybot</a> and choose Premium.</li>
      <li>Pick a term — 3, 6 or 12 months — and enter your username.</li>
      <li>Transfer the exact amount shown from Click, Payme, Uzum or your bank app.</li>
      <li>Press "I have paid". Premium reactivates in about 10 seconds and Telegram sends its own notification.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Prices: 172,000 UZS for 3 months, 232,000 for 6, 422,000 for 12. Step-by-step with screenshots: <a href="/en/how-to-buy">how to buy</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Renewing early vs letting it lapse</h2>
    <p>If you buy a new term while the current one is still running, the time adds on rather than replacing it — you do not lose the remaining days. So there is no reason to wait until the last moment if you know you are continuing.</p>
    <p>If you let it lapse for a while and come back later, nothing is penalised. There is no reactivation fee and no lost state; you simply pick up where you left off.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>One thing worth checking first</h2>
    <p>If Premium ended without you expecting it, check whether it was originally bought as an <strong>auto-renewing subscription through the App Store or Google Play</strong>. Those renew from a card and fail silently when the card expires or has insufficient funds. If that is what happened, either fix the card there or switch to one-off purchases — with a reseller nothing is charged in the background, which some people prefer precisely because there is no surprise.</p>
  </section>

